    "summary": "I fixed an off-by-one error in `stats/window.py`. The loop used `range(len(values) - window)`, which stops one starting position too early, so the last window was never averaged. A list of length `n` has `n - window + 1` windows, so I changed the loop to `range(len(values) - window + 1)`.\n\n`moving_average([1, 2, 3, 4], 2)` now returns `[1.5, 2.5, 3.5]`. The signature is the same, and the `ValueError` for `window < 1` still works. If `window` is longer than the list, the range is empty and the fu",
